    "id": "thm:constructive-completeness",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Suppose \\(S_k=\\{j\\}\\), where \\(j\\in\\{k,k+1\\}\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,T\\}\\), and \\(S_t=\\varnothing\\) for \\(t\\ne k\\). Then \\(\\mathsf C_1=1\\) if and only if \\(\\mathcal H(B)\\ne\\varnothing\\), if and only if \\(\\operatorname{GID}(T,S,B)=1\\). The affirmative branch returns the explicit reconstruction and the negative branch returns the positive witness, uniformly over all positive laws, null allowed-arrow effects, and deficient transition ranks.",
